---Store authentication credentials for a catalog. These credentials are used to authenticate with R2 storage when performing catalog operations.
---
---`POST /accounts/{account_id}/r2-catalog/{bucket_name}/credential`
---Errors: InvalidRoute, InvalidCredential.
---@param input cloudflare.r2_data_catalog.CreateCredentialRequest
---@return any? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_credential(input) end

---Removes the catalog from the control plane without deleting R2 bucket objects. Set force=true to remove catalog namespaces, tables, views, and maintenance metadata. Force deletion is limited to a configured catalog object count.
---
---`POST /accounts/{account_id}/r2-catalog/{bucket_name}/delete`
---@param input cloudflare.r2_data_catalog.DeleteRequest
---@return cloudflare.r2_data_catalog.DeleteResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:delete(input) end

---Disable an R2 bucket as a catalog. This operation deactivates the catalog but preserves existing metadata and data files. The catalog can be re-enabled later.
---
---`POST /accounts/{account_id}/r2-catalog/{bucket_name}/disable`
---Errors: NoSuchBucket, InvalidRoute, WarehouseNotFound, Forbidden.
---@param input cloudflare.r2_data_catalog.DisableR2DataCatalogRequest
---@return cloudflare.r2_data_catalog.DisableR2DataCatalogResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:disable_r2_data_catalog(input) end

---Enable an R2 bucket as an Apache Iceberg catalog. This operation creates the necessary catalog infrastructure and activates the bucket for storing Iceberg metadata and data files.
---
---`POST /accounts/{account_id}/r2-catalog/{bucket_name}/enable`
---Errors: NoSuchBucket, InvalidRoute.
